  "description": "Serial port I/O that does one job well: cancellable, deadline-honouring reads and writes that never abort spuriously (the CH34x ERROR_OPERATION_ABORTED trap of System.IO.Ports async reads), a bounded open and close, typed failures (timeout with the partial reply, framing, device removed, port busy, I/O the driver never completed), and port enumeration with a stable hardware identity (USB VID/PID, serial number, socket location).",
